 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway Instances API](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-servers-list-servers).
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # project_id is the mandatory id of the Scaleway project (or organization) to discover instances in.
+    #
+  - project_id: "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
+
+    # zone is an optional Scaleway availability zone to discover instances in.
+    # By default, "fr-par-1" is used.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/console/account/reference-content/products-availability/
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # api_url is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Scaleway API requires a secret key to be sent in every request via the `X-Auth-Token` HTTP header.
+    # It can be created at https://console.scaleway.com/project/credentials
+    # and configured via the `headers` option below.
+    #
+    headers:
+    - "X-Auth-Token: xxxx-secret-key-xxxx"
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<ip>:<port>`, where `<ip>` is the public IPv4 address of the instance if it has one, or its private IPv4 address otherwise,
+while `<port>` is the port specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs`.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the availability zone of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the state of the instance, e.g. `running`, `stopped`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the instance, e.g. `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma separated list of tags applied to the instance.
+
+Instances without a public or a private IPv4 address are skipped, since there is no address to scrape.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
